<div class="cn-legal-content"><section class="cn-legal-section" id="summary">
<h2>1. Policy summary</h2>
<p>CyberNet AI Pro is a recurring monthly or yearly subscription. It renews automatically until cancelled. The amount and interval are shown before checkout. Unless applicable law or an approved exception requires otherwise, payments are non-refundable after a billing period begins. The CyberNet AI iPhone app has no purchases; this policy covers plans bought on the website.</p>
</section>
<section class="cn-legal-section" id="billing">
<h2>2. Billing authorisation</h2>
<p>By selecting Pro and accepting the checkout disclosure, you authorise Stripe and CyberNet to charge the selected payment method for the initial term and each renewal. Monthly subscriptions are currently advertised at USD $9.99 per month and yearly subscriptions at USD $95.90 per year unless checkout clearly shows another amount.</p>
</section>
<section class="cn-legal-section" id="cancel">
<h2>3. How to cancel</h2>
<p>Cancel through <strong>Account → Manage Billing</strong>. If the billing portal is unavailable, contact <a href="mailto:support@cybernetai.app">support@cybernetai.app</a> before the next renewal and include the account email. Cancellation normally takes effect at the end of the current paid term.</p>
<p><strong>Deleting your account cancels your subscription immediately.</strong> If you delete your CyberNet account, on the website or in the iPhone app, while a subscription can still renew or be charged, including the subscription of a Business team you own, CyberNet cancels it at once as part of the deletion. Paid access ends immediately, and no refund, credit or proration is given for the rest of the current billing period, except as described in sections 6 and 12. To keep paid access until the end of the period you have paid for, cancel through Manage Billing first and delete your account after that date.</p>
</section>
<section class="cn-legal-section" id="access">
<h2>4. Access after cancellation</h2>
<p>Unless checkout or applicable law states otherwise, Pro access continues until the end of the paid billing period. After that, the account returns to Free and Pro-only history, downloads, or planned features may become unavailable.</p>
<p><strong>Business team accounts.</strong> A Business subscription is owned by the team owner, and only the owner can cancel it. When a Business subscription is cancelled or lapses, Business access ends at the close of the paid period for <strong>the owner and every member of that team at the same time</strong>, or immediately if the owner deletes their account. Each member's account then returns to whatever plan it independently holds, which for most members is Free. Members cannot cancel the team subscription, and a member leaving the team does not cancel or reduce the owner's subscription — the seat simply becomes free for someone else. Removing a member takes effect immediately and does not generate a refund or proration for the remainder of the paid period.</p>
</section>
<section class="cn-legal-section" id="refund-rule">
<h2>5. General refund rule</h2>
<p>CyberNet generally does not provide refunds, credits, or prorated amounts for unused time, accidental non-use, a changed decision, failure to cancel before renewal, or features clearly described as coming soon or concept previews.</p>
</section>
<section class="cn-legal-section" id="eligible">
<h2>6. Situations that may qualify</h2>
<p>CyberNet may approve a refund for a duplicate charge, confirmed billing error, unauthorised transaction after reasonable verification, a material failure to provide purchased access, or another situation required by applicable law. Approval is case-specific and does not create a continuing obligation.</p>
</section>
<section class="cn-legal-section" id="request">
<h2>7. Requesting a refund</h2>
<p>Contact support promptly with the account email, charge date, amount, last four card digits if appropriate, and a clear explanation. Do not send complete card details, passwords, one-time codes, or identity documents unless support provides a secure and lawful method.</p>
</section>
<section class="cn-legal-section" id="timing">
<h2>8. Processing time</h2>
<p>Approved refunds are submitted to Stripe promptly. The bank or payment provider controls when funds appear, which may take several business days. CyberNet is not responsible for bank processing times.</p>
</section>
<section class="cn-legal-section" id="currency">
<h2>9. Currency, taxes, and conversion</h2>
<p>Prices are displayed in the stated currency. Banks may apply exchange rates, international fees, taxes, or other charges that CyberNet does not control and normally cannot refund.</p>
</section>
<section class="cn-legal-section" id="chargebacks">
<h2>10. Chargebacks and disputes</h2>
<p>Contact CyberNet first so a billing error can be investigated. This does not limit lawful rights to contact a bank or dispute an unauthorised charge. CyberNet may provide checkout, acceptance, usage, cancellation, and account records to the payment provider when responding to a dispute.</p>
</section>
<section class="cn-legal-section" id="promotions">
<h2>11. Trials, discounts, and promotions</h2>
<p>Promotional prices, coupons, and trials may have specific terms shown at checkout. Unless stated otherwise, a discounted subscription renews at the then-current standard price after the promotional period.</p>
</section>
<section class="cn-legal-section" id="rights">
<h2>12. Mandatory rights and contact</h2>
<p>Nothing in this Policy excludes a refund, cancellation, withdrawal, or remedy that cannot lawfully be excluded. Billing and cancellation support: <a href="mailto:support@cybernetai.app">support@cybernetai.app</a>.</p>
</section></div>
